---
# Reusable content component (dsl §13). A component FILE declares `component:`
# (its name) + optional `params:` (typed exactly like a scene `defs` param,
# §8.1). The body is a PRESENTATIONAL template: lines + staging directives +
# `@param` refs — no state read/write, and no logic block EXCEPT a param-scoped
# `<match on="@param">`, which dsl 0.4.0 §6.2 admits (dispatching on an
# invocation argument reads no ambient state and records nothing; see
# `reaction.component.lute`). `<branch>`/`<hub>` stay forbidden on principle —
# presenting a menu records the selection into `scene.choices.*`, a state write.
# It is imported by a scene via `components: [..]` and expanded inline by
# `::use`.
component: greet
params:
  who: string
# A component's own vocabulary import (dsl 0.9.0). It makes a STANDALONE
# `lute check` of this file resolve `action=`; through `::use` the IMPORTING
# document's vocabulary is the one that applies (see 0.9.0 §5, known
# limitation), so both sides declare it.
uses: ../base.schema.yaml
---

## A Familiar Face

/* `@who` is the param, bound to the `::use` arg at expansion time; it is legal
   here only because `character` is a `string`-typed attr (dsl Appendix A). */
::auto{character=@who action="fade-in-up"}
@narrator: A familiar face steps into the light.
